add(1517,'hamming-end','Hamming endpoint conflict','Using the printed periodic Hamming equation w[n] = 0.54 − 0.46 cos(2πn/L), what is w[0]?',[
('0.08, so the claim that this Hamming window reaches zero at the boundary is false.','cos(0)=1 gives 0.54−0.46.'),('0, agreeing exactly with a zero-endpoint claim.','This subtracts 0.54 rather than the printed 0.46 coefficient.'),('1, because every window endpoint is its maximum.','The maximum occurs near the center, not at n=0.'),('0.54, because the cosine term vanishes at n=0.','cos(0)=1, not zero.')],'The periodic formula is meaningful, but its first weight is nonzero. It must not be silently replaced by a Hann window.',typ='numerical',kind='equation',steps=['w[0] = 0.54 − 0.46 × 1 = 0.08.'],formulas=[FHAM],conflict='The accompanying prose says Hamming smoothly reaches zero at the boundaries, contradicting its printed formula.',external=['hamming'],locator='Hamming formula and zero-boundary prose.')
